    \page tutorial-game-end.html
    \title Tutorial 11: Ending the Match
    \previouspage {Tutorial 10: AI Opponents and Wildlife}

    \section1 Rules

    A destroyed base knocks its race out and kills its creatures. Troll lairs do not count.
    After each destroyed base the core checks:

    \quotefromfile backend/game.cpp
    \skipto if (!player_base_alive) {
    \printuntil }
    \printuntil }

    Ending the match stops wildlife and all order queues, then reports the result:

    \quotefromfile backend/game.cpp
    \skipto void game_t::end_match(bool victory_p)
    \printuntil }
    \printuntil }

    \section1 The game over scene

    QML gets the \c matchEnded signal and switches state:

    \quotefromfile qml/Main.qml
    \skipto function onMatchEnded(victory, durationMs) {
    \printuntil }

    \c GameOverScene is a third scene with a see through background, so the battle stays
    visible behind it. Two \c AppButton items offer \uicontrol {Play again} and
    \uicontrol {Main menu}.

    \image readme-victory.png
    \caption Victory.

    \section1 Effects with EntityManager

    Mages hit a 3 by 3 area. Each hit spawns a short explosion through Felgo's
    \c EntityManager:

    \quotefromfile qml/components/WorldMap.qml
    \skipto function showAreaAttack(column, row, radius, color) {
    \printuntil })

    The explosion is an \c EntityBase that removes itself when its animation ends:

    \quotefromfile qml/components/AreaExplosion.qml
    \skipto ScriptAction {
    \printuntil }

